Third-party components: wgpu, naga, wasm-bindgen, js-sys, web-sys, bytemuck, serde, serde_json (MIT or Apache-2.0); three.js (MIT); Pyodide (MPL-2.0, loaded unmodified from its npm package for the embedded Python console); FastAPI (MIT); Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause); python-multipart (Apache-2.0); OpenColorIO with its built-in ACES configs (BSD-3-Clause, used through the opencolorio Python package in the service); xterm.js and its fit addon (MIT) for the terminal dock; Inter and JetBrains Mono through Fontsource (SIL Open Font License 1.1); ptyprocess (ISC) and pywinpty (MIT) for terminal sessions; Tauri and its shell, dialog and updater plugins (MIT or Apache-2.0) for the desktop app. PyInstaller (GPL-2.0 with its bootloader exception) is a build tool only: it packs the service into the desktop sidecar and its license allows distributing the frozen result under FormSurface's own terms. The terminal dock, chat pane, command registry and menu code follow formlit and formvis, sibling nodemode-ai projects under the same Apache-2.0 license.
Projection painting follows the published approach of rasterizing the mesh in UV space and testing texels in world space (Schaerfig and Hormann, VMV 2010); no third-party painting code is copied.
